x86_64-windows  refused for a reason older than this case and unrelated to dynamic_cast: `Both` has virtual functions in a base that is not the first, which the Microsoft ABI lays out differently and cxx1 already refuses by name. `dynamic_cast<void *>` itself is NOT refused for this target - it emits `call __RTCastToVoid`, and dynamic-cast-void.cpp exercises it here. This file exists only for the negative-offset path, which needs the layout the refusal blocks.
